 "drivers": "Democrats won control of both the House and Senate, setting up a divided government. Futures swung from steep overnight losses (S&P −1.2%, Nasdaq-100 −2% per IC Markets) to gains after President Trump struck a conciliatory tone, with the Dow now leading at about +2%. Tech is lagging on worries about tighter scrutiny of AI and data-center build-outs, and Texas elected Democrat Gina Hinojosa as governor after she pledged a moratorium on new data-center construction; chips, AI-hosting miners (CIFR, HUT, CLSK, IREN), CoreWeave and Texas power names (VST) are lower, and Tesla and SpaceX are down 5–6% given Elon Musk's large GOP spending. The dollar is weaker, gold is up almost 3% above $4,050, WTI is down about 2% on signs of US–Iran de-escalation, and the VIX has dropped back below 20. Data today includes ADP payrolls, final S&P PMIs and ISM services; CVS plans to split into two companies.",
